  // ============================================================================
  // Root Cause Analysis: Fault Attribution & Building a Bulletproof Path Resolver
  // ============================================================================
  //
  // WHOSE FAULT IS IT?
  // It’s a shared failure across three distinct layers:
  // 1. Cargo: Emits ambiguous, context-dependent relative paths instead of absolute
  //    URIs or fully qualified diagnostic footprints.
  // 2. VS Code Core: Relies on rigid regex matching for terminal text streams without
  //    a built-in fallback heuristic or workspace-relative path normalization pass.
  // 3. The Extension Ecosystem: Naively concatenates variables (`${workspaceFolder}`)
  //    without validating whether the resulting URI actually resolves to a real inode
  //    on disk, leading to silent failures or double-nested paths.
  //
  // HOW TO BUILD A BULLETPROOF SYSTEM (IDE / Terminal Link Engine):
  // Your instinct is spot on. Instead of blindly gluing strings together, a truly
  // resilient path resolution engine should implement a defensive lookup strategy:
  //
  // 1. Extraction & Normalization:
  //    - Parse the captured string from the CLI output.
  //    - Strip out diagnostic artifacts (leading arrows, spacing, column/row suffixes).
  //
  // 2. Multi-Tier Path Resolution (The Recursive / Heuristic Fallback):
  //    - Tier 1 (Direct Match): Test if the path exists as-is relative to the CWD.
  //    - Tier 2 (Workspace Anchor): Test against the absolute workspace root.
  //    - Tier 3 (Recursive Suffix Clipping - Your Idea): If the file doesn't exist,
  //      start stripping leading path segments one by one (e.g., dropping `crates/learn/`)
  //      and search outward or walk up the directory tree from the CWD until a
  //      matching filename and relative suffix is found on disk.
  //
  // 3. Validation Guard:
  //    - Never emit a `vscode://file/...` URI blindly. Always verify `fs::metadata`
  //      on the target path *before* letting the editor attempt navigation. If validation
  //      fails, fall back to a fuzzy workspace symbol search rather than throwing a dead link.
  // ============================================================================
